# kv4-edge-inference — environment config (copy to config/local.env and edit).
# The example values describe the paper's reference rig: NVIDIA GTX 1650
# (TU117, sm_75, 4 GB, GDDR6/192 GB/s). Adjust every path for your machine.

# --- llama.cpp build (TheTom/llama-cpp-turboquant fork; see README) ----------
LLAMA_BIN_DIR=/opt/llama-cpp-turboquant/build/bin   # dir with llama-bench, llama-server, …
CUDA_LIB=/usr/local/cuda/lib64                       # CUDA runtime libs (match your version)

# --- models (Q4_K_M GGUF) ----------------------------------------------------
MODEL_DIR=/opt/models
MODEL_QWEN3=qwen3-1.7b.gguf
MODEL_LLAMA32=llama32-3b.gguf
MODEL_SMOLLM2=smollm2-1.7b.gguf
MODEL_MINICPM=minicpm5-1b.gguf

# --- run controls ------------------------------------------------------------
WORK_DIR=./kv4-evidence        # where measured evidence is written
REPS=5                         # llama-bench repetitions per cell
PORT=11437                     # llama-server port for VRAM / RAG arms
CLOCK_LOCK=tdp                 # nvidia-smi --lock-gpu-clocks value (tdp, or "base,base", or MHz)
VRAM_SERVICE=ollama            # local service to stop so it can't co-reside in VRAM ("" = skip)
NCU_BIN=                       # path to Nsight Compute `ncu` for the L4 profile ("" = skip)

# --- RAG arm (realistic retrieval) -------------------------------------------
EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text   # Ollama embedding model for retrieval (mirrors Shaik 2025)
RAG_CORPUS=                    # path to YOUR corpus .txt (we cannot ship the paper's; see rag/)
